            "Chip War: The Fight for the World's Most Critical Technology",
            "Chris Miller is a professor at the Fletcher School of Law and Diplomacy of Tufts University.",
            "Chris Miller wrote the book \"Chip War: The Fight for the World's Most Critical Technology\".",
            "In the book, Chris Miller argues that the next era, including the rivalry between the US and China, will be all about computing power.",
            "Chris Miller outlines the nature of the coming battle over semiconductors.",
            "Chris Miller defines how the power to produce leading-edge chips fell into the hands of just five companies: three from the US, one from Japan and one from the Netherlands.",
            "In an interview with \"Protocol\", Chris Miller argues that semiconductors are used to integrate new munitions and transfer information between them.",
            "Chris Miller argues that advanced semiconductors are necessary at every stage of the process of developing new munitions."
